    "content": "<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/SSA101/flm1/d37/001.webp\" alt=\"SSA101 · 36. Project Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation · slide 1: Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">36. Project Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation · slide 1/8</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation<br>ACADEMIC DEVELOPMENT GROUP PROJECT</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/SSA101/flm1/d37/002.webp\" alt=\"SSA101 · 36. Project Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation · slide 2: Plan of Project – Writing Guide\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">36. Project Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation · slide 2/8</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Plan of Project – Writing Guide<br>1. Project Overview<br>Briefly introduce the project topic<br>State the problem or need being addressed<br>2. Objectives<br>Define clear, measurable goals<br>Explain what the project aims to achieve<br>3. Target Audience<br>Identify who will benefit from the project<br>Describe their needs and relevance<br>4. Implementation Plan<br>Key activities and timeline<br>Roles and responsibilities<br>Tools, methods, and resources<br>5. Expected Outcomes<br>Project deliverables<br>Impact on students or learning environment<br>6. Evaluation Plan<br>How success will be measured<br>Data collection or feedback methods</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/SSA101/flm1/d37/003.webp\" alt=\"SSA101 · 36. Project Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation · slide 3: 5. Feedback Collection\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">36. Project Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation · slide 3/8</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>5. Feedback Collection<br>Evaluation Focus:<br>Analyze feedback from team members and beneficiaries.<br>Evaluation Criteria:<br>Satisfaction level (e.g., ≥ 80% positive feedback).<br>Consistency of feedback themes.<br>Constructiveness: feedback includes suggestions for improvement.<br>Timeliness: feedback collected promptly during implementation.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/SSA101/flm1/d37/004.webp\" alt=\"SSA101 · 36. Project Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation · slide 4: 6. Gap Analysis\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">36. Project Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation · slide 4/8</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>6. Gap Analysis<br>Evaluation Focus:<br>Identify deviations from the plan and determine underlying causes.<br>Evaluation Criteria:<br>Clear documentation of deviations (delays, quality issues, resource shortages).<br>Categorization of severity:<br>Minor (no major impact)<br>Moderate (requires adjustment)<br>Severe (threatens success)<br>Accurate identification of root causes.<br>Feasible corrective actions proposed.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/SSA101/flm1/d37/005.webp\" alt=\"SSA101 · 36. Project Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation · slide 5: 7. Risk Management Plan\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">36. Project Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation · slide 5/8</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>7. Risk Management Plan<br>Includes:<br>Potential risks that may occur during the implementation process<br>The level of impact and the likelihood of each risk<br>Preventive measures and response plans<br>Example: Lack of Supplies or Donations.<br>Potential Risk: Materials (e.g., food, books, gifts) or financial donations are not enough for the activity.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/SSA101/flm1/d37/006.webp\" alt=\"SSA101 · 36. Project Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation · slide 6: 8. Risk Management Guide\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">36. Project Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation · slide 6/8</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>8. Risk Management Guide<br>1. Identify Potential Risks:<br>Determine risks that may occur during implementation.<br>Examples: low volunteer turnout, lack of supplies, bad weather, timeline delays.<br>2. Assess Impact &amp; Likelihood:<br>Evaluate impact level (low–medium–high).<br>Evaluate likelihood (rare–possible–likely).<br>Prioritize high-impact or high-likelihood risks.<br>3. Develop Preventive Measures:<br>Create plans to reduce the chance of risks occurring.<br>Examples: early volunteer recruitment, weekly supply tracking.<br>4. Prepare Response Plans:<br>Define actions to take if risks materialize.<br>Examples: scaling down activities, seeking extra support, adjusting timelines.<br>5. Assign Responsibilities:<br>Specify who monitors each risk.<br>Identify decision-makers for activating response plans.<br>6. Monitor &amp; Update:<br>Continuously track risks during implementation.<br>Update plans when new risks arise or conditions change.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/SSA101/flm1/d37/007.webp\" alt=\"SSA101 · 36. Project Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation · slide 7: Key Considerations for Later Project Stages\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">36. Project Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation · slide 7/8</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Key Considerations for Later Project Stages<br>1. Maintain Clear Communication:<br>Keep all stakeholders updated on progress and changes.<br>Schedule regular check-ins to avoid misunderstandings.<br>2. Monitor Resource Usage:<br>Ensure budget, materials, and manpower remain sufficient.<br>Adjust allocations as project demands evolve.<br>3. Evaluate Progress Against Goals:<br>Compare achievements with planned milestones.<br>Identify gaps early to take corrective action.<br>4. Prepare for Unexpected Changes:<br>Anticipate potential challenges in later phases.<br>Have contingency plans ready for timeline or resource issues.<br>5. Sustain Team Motivation:<br>Recognize contributions and keep morale high.<br>Address burnout or workload imbalance promptly.<br>6. Document Everything:<br>Keep detailed records for reporting and future learning.<br>Ensure transparency and accountability.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/SSA101/flm1/d37/008.webp\" alt=\"SSA101 · 36. Project Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation · slide 8\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">36. Project Evaluation Framework for Phase 4 Implementation · slide 8/8</p></div>"
